i love cheesecake a lot of people love  cheesecake i love cookies and cream a  lot of people love cookies and cream so  i had this idea of making a cookies and  cream cheesecake that was just purely  black and white but had the cleanest  layers possible during my time at tasty  i've gone through a lot of phases there  was you know the giant food phase and at  one point reoccurring phase was the  layer phase i  absolutely love layers i think they're  beautiful i think that can be really  cool very visual the thought process was  that i would take you know the base  would be the cookies the filling would  be the cheesecake that also uses the  fillings from the cookies and the top  would be a thin layer of like those like  pulverized like ground or fine powdered  of the cookies so you get like a black  white black look so pretty much is you  start with the base you make the filling  and then do the top so the base is just  crushed pulverized cookies that you mix  with some butter  [Music]  you bake it like a graham cracker crust  it's pretty simple you just put it in  and bake it you kind of really want to  press it flat so there's no huge lumps  [Music]  so that goes in and after you separate  the filling from the cookies you want to  save the cookie filling to make sure  that you can use that for your  cheesecake filling you mix that with  some cream cheese and it's a pretty  standard cheesecake batter recipe what  makes this a no-bake recipe is that it  uses gelatin to help set the mixture so  gelatin mixture is then whisked back in  to the cheesecake mixture so it creates  this really smooth really nice really  velvety kind of texture that also has  the melted cookie filling in it so you  don't really waste anything here it's  kind of you know you separate the cookie  into the crust you separate the filling  into the cheesecake it's basically  you're redefining the shape of what the  cookie looked like in the first place  once that filling is set you want to  pour that into the  baked cheesecake mold and that kind of  sets in the fridge you want to make sure  that it's as smooth as possible no lumps  if you really need to and you see lumps  and flecks of stuff  you can sieve it you can patch it  through a mesh sieve to get rid of any  impurities if you really want to that  goes in the fridge for a very long time  if you actually want the cleanest layers  possible you can throw it in the freezer  it's not going to make a difference the  taste and the texture because by the  time you serve it it's going to be cold  anyways and the reason why i didn't bake  this one is because when you bake a  cheesecake  i'm maybe i'm not good at it but i found  it pretty difficult to get like this  perfect smooth like top layer with no  bumps no dips no crevices or anything so  i went for the no bake route so this  recipe is pretty simple and the key i  think to really getting those clean  layers is after the whole thing is done  you do want to put it back into the  fridge or the freezer if you put it in  the freezer you will get the sharpest  cleanest layers possible this is one of  my personal secrets for cutting cakes  cutting cheesecakes cutting pies is  either freezing them or semi-freezing  them because the knife goes through it  goes straight down it doesn't bend it  doesn't really drag on anything it  really helps give you those nice clean  layers so it's a play on a cheesecake  that i think was very fun it satisfied  my layer cravings at the time  although i definitely made a lot more  layered stuff after that but it is a fun  recipe it doesn't require too much  cooking too much baking it is a no-bake  cheesecake so you don't actually have to  use your oven which i think is pretty  cool because i don't have an oven at  home and it's just an all-around recipe  that pretty much everybody is going to  like so if you do make it for a party  it's a crowd pleaser i guarantee people  are going to enjoy it you do make it let  me know i think 